Your provided MATLAB code is efficient for finding the unique words in Text1 that do not appear in Text2. It uses built-in functions like `fileread()`, `lower()`, `strsplit()`, and `setdiff()` to perform the task. This implementation can handle a large amount of text as it reads the text files directly and processes them efficiently.

To further optimize the code, you can consider using a more memory-efficient data structure like a hash table (also known as a dictionary or map) instead of a set for storing unique words. Here's an updated version of your code using a hash table:

```matlab
text1 = fileread('Text1.txt'); %read text1 from file
text2 = fileread('Text2.txt'); %read text2 from file

%Convert text to lowercase and split into words
words1 = lower(strsplit(text1));
words2 = lower(strsplit(text2));

%Create a hash table to store unique words from Text1
uniqueWords1 = cellfun(@(w) w, unique(words1), 'UniformOutput', false);
uniqueWords1 = table(uniqueWords1, ...
    'VariableNames', {'Word'}, ...
    'Class', {'string'});

%Check if each word from Text2 is present in Text1's unique words
